		//    look friendly" — and the machinery agrees: `organizerOutlineProps`
		//    holds FRONTMATTER KEYS and `orgFieldRow` draws frontmatter.
		//    Pressing ▤ on a reading put `words` into that set; measured, the
		//    set came back `['synopsis','words']`. So a reading's ▤ is DRAWN
		//    AND DEAD rather than absent — remove it and the toggle column
		//    goes ragged, and the two columns stop reading as two questions
		//    asked of every row.
		//
		// 4. …EXCEPT `tags`, WHICH IS HONESTLY BOTH. It is a built-in column
		//    AND a real frontmatter key with its own chips in the Outline;
