					// THE EXPORT ARROW POINTS AWAY FROM THE PAGE (writer,
					// 2026-08-22: the Organizer's export icon was "mirrored"
					// against the Word-Smith menu's). Measured live: the menu
					// draws `file-output` under `.zg-menu-icon.is-mirrored`
					// and computes matrix(-1,0,0,1,0,0); this tab drew the
					// same glyph with no flip, so the two pointed opposite
					// ways. Lucide draws this family pointing LEFT and the
					// menu has always flipped it - so the tab joins the menu
					// rather than the menu giving up its flip.
					//
					// GATED ON THE DRAWN NAME, not on the row id, which is
					// how the menu does it: the alts chain can fall through to
